# Bridge reassembler hygiene fix (RCA fix #3, docs/chunk-loss-rca-2026-11-02.md).
# Bug reproduced against the live handler: an aborted run's chunks survive in
# _pending; a later run reusing the same image id fills its gaps with the stale
# chunks and _save_streaming_png saves a splice (test: saved == B0+A1+B2).
# Fix: (1) seq-0 for an id with existing chunks resets the stream;
# (2) strict base64 validation per chunk (truncated b64 now poisons/drops the
# stream instead of silently decoding short); (3) save requires seqs starting
# at 0 with no gaps and CLEARS _pending on any validation failure;
# (4) full PNG chunk walk with CRC verification before saving.
# Validated offline: splice scenario -> old saves splice, patched refuses;
# clean complete PNG -> both save byte-identical. Apply + restart subscriber
# only on John's go, ideally between bench sessions.
